    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0652" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p1/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">771.00/12–1452: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        France</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d309-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret
                        priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-12-15T18:01:00-05:00">December 15, 1952—6:01
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3401. Supplementing Tangier Legtel 240, Dec.
                        14,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d309-f2"/> 35 to Paris, Balafredj has informed
                        USUN official that he reed msg Sun from Sultan than remaining Istiqlal leaders
                    have been rounded up and he himself is in imminent danger being deposed. Dept queried Con
                    Rabat Sun this matter.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d309-f3"/></p>
                <p>Today USUN reports that Balafredj is
                    broadcasting this news at UN and that Indo Rep
                    mentioned it this morning in UN debate. La-Coste says story is nonsense but that he is not in position
                    make official statement for Fr Govt. USUN also
                    reports Balafredj addressing plea to Secy on this subj.</p>
                <p>In light of foregoing, Secy may wish take occasion when mtg with Schuman to express informally opinion that
                    recent Fr public disavowal of intention to depose Bey of Tunis is having quieting effect on North Af situation and that he presumes Fr Govt entertains
                    similar intention toward Sultan of Morocco. Since we understand from USUN that tone Morocco debate more serious in
                    criticism of Fr than Tunisian discussion,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d309-f4"/>
                    presumably Fr public statement denying rumor of plans to depose Sultan wld be
                    even more useful. Since in absence of Fr from North Af debates in UN US has had to accept more active role in debate
                    than we wld have desired, we feel justified approaching Fr this matter.</p>
                <p>If Secy approves this suggestion, he may prefer have Emb approach FonOff in this
                    vein.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Bruce</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d309-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d309-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was drafted by Cyr (AF) and cleared in EUR and NEA. Matthews (G)
                    signed for the Acting Secretary. It was repeated to Tangier, Rabat, and
                    Casablanca.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d309-f2" n="2" xml:id="d309-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d308"><ref target="#d308"><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Supra</hi></ref></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d309-f3" n="3" xml:id="d309-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 53 to Rabat, Dec. 14, not printed. (771.00/12–1452)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d309-f4" n="4" xml:id="d309-f4-content">
                <p>For the documentation on Tunisia, see <ref target="#pg665">pp. 665</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
